      "document_text": "OANDA Canada's official financing page says positions open at 5pm ET are treated as overnight and may incur a charge or credit. FX, gold and silver daily financing is position size multiplied by applicable annualized rate divided by 365; index financing is position value multiplied by rate divided by 365. Long and short rates differ and may change daily. FX, gold and silver rates use liquidity-provider tom-next swaps plus instrument-specific admin fee. Index long rates include a 2.5% admin fee plus the relevant alternative reference rate; short rates use the difference between the reference rate and 2.5%, producing a charge or credit depending on the relationship. FX, gold and silver typically settle T+2, so Wednesday financing is usually tripled; index weekend financing is typically tripled Friday, subject to holidays. Indicative current-day rates are not finalized until 5pm ET.",
