      "document_text": "OANDA Canada's FAQ defines Margin Close-Out Percentage as (50% × Margin Used) / NAV_mid, with values up to 100% as the closeout trigger. A margin call occurs when NAV_mid falls below Margin Used; the account is checked at 3:45 p.m. ET. If the account remains under-margined for six consecutive trading days, all open positions are automatically closed at current OANDA rates. If NAV_mid falls to half or less of Margin Used (Margin Close-Out Percentage ≥100%), all open positions are automatically closed at current rates. Positions whose markets are unavailable remain open and monitored; another closeout may occur when markets reopen if the account remains under-margined. The FAQ warns that fast markets may leave little or no time for alerts.",
