      "document_text": "OANDA's official v20 Order Definitions identify the supported order types (Market, FixedPrice, Limit, Stop, MarketIfTouched, TakeProfit, StopLoss, GuaranteedStopLoss and TrailingStopLoss). Pending orders expose an order ID, state, type, instrument and order-specific fields. Entry orders include signed units and positionFill. Trade-dependent TakeProfit, StopLoss, GuaranteedStopLoss and TrailingStopLoss orders carry tradeID. The API defines positionFill OPEN_ONLY as opening/extending positions, REDUCE_FIRST as reducing existing positions before opening a new position, REDUCE_ONLY as reducing an existing position only, and DEFAULT as REDUCE_FIRST for non-client-hedging accounts or OPEN_ONLY for client-hedging accounts.",
